{0 Eio tmux clients}

{!Libtmux_eio.Client} uses the application's switch, process manager and
monotonic clock. The library never starts an Eio scheduler. Live handles belong
to the connecting domain; immutable captured observations can be shared.

{1 Keep the operation handle}

Submit before awaiting. {!Libtmux_eio.Operation} retains success, failure or
uncertainty when a waiter is cancelled. Client-owned workers continue draining
admitted requests. An acknowledgement alone does not establish task completion.

{1 Observe without blocking delivery}

{!Libtmux_eio.Subscription} uses bounded subscriber queues and client-owned
readers. A stalled consumer cannot block an independent subscriber or command.
Gaps end continuity; recovery is explicit. Byte cursors do not establish a
snapshot/history barrier.

Use {!Libtmux_eio.Client.wait_for_text} for a level-triggered rendered-screen
condition, and {!Libtmux_eio.Subscription.wait_for_bytes} for future raw bytes.
